Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall begin not later than three years from the date of this decision.
Reason: In order to comply with Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990, as amended by Section 51 of the Planning and Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.
Condition : 2 - The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans and specifications: 
Drawings PL-01(Rev.A), PL-14(Rev.E), PL-15(Rev.B), PL-16(Rev.B), PL-17(Rev.B) and 012-PL-GA-101(Rev.04), received 14/05/2026. Transport Statement (Version 4, dated April 2026), Tree Constraints Plan (Drawing TCP01, Rev.01) and Tree Schedule (dated 21/04/2026), received 05/05/2026. Drawings PL-10, PL-11, PL-12 and PL-13 and Air Quality Assessment (dated P9550-R2-V1, Version 1, dated 30/01/2026), Car Parking, Delivery & Servicing Management Plan (EA/25:413, dated January 2026), Construction Method Statement & Traffic Management Plan (EA/25:413, dated January 2026), Energy and Sustainability Statement (Version 1, dated 12/01/2026), Fire Safety Statement (Version 1.0, dated January 2026), Internal Daylight & Sunlight Report (2040/D rev-, dated January 2026), Marketing Letter (undated and unreferenced), MEP Planning Stage Report with appendices (25324, Rev.00, dated January 2026), Noise Impact Assessment Report (P9550-R1-V1, Version 1, dated 30/01/2026), Planning, Design and Access Statement (dated 09/02/2026), Preliminary Ecological Appraisal (Version 1.0, dated 12/01/2026), Sustainable Drainage Assessment (FRE/2026/LR6/SDA, dated January 2026) and pro forma, Utility Statement (25324, Rev.00, dated January 2026) and Ventilation and Extraction Report (25324, Rev.00, dated January 2026), all received 18/02/2026.
Reason: In order to ensure the development is carried out in accordance with the planning permission.
Condition : 3 - Notwithstanding the provisions of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development Order) 1995 (or any order revoking or re-enacting that order), no further enlargement or alteration of the premises or erection of any additional structures/buildings/enclosures within the curtilage of the site shall be carried out, other than as shown in the approved drawings, and no additional floor space shall be formed within the buildings hereby permitted by means of internal horizontal division (e.g. new mezzanine levels) without prior written approval of the local planning authority. 
No cables, wires, aerials, pipework (except any rainwater downpipes as may be shown on the approved drawings), meter boxes or flues shall be fixed to any elevation facing a highway.
Reason:  To protect neighbours' living conditions and the character and appearance of the area and to prevent over-intensive use of the site.
Condition : 4 - (a) The development hereby permitted shall be implemented in accordance with the approved Energy Strategy.
(b) Prior to first occupation of any unit within the development hereby approved, evidence (e.g. photographs, installation contracts and As-Built certificates under the Standard Assessment Procedure/National Calculation Method) shall be submitted to the local planning authority and approved in writing to show that the development has been constructed in accordance with the approved Energy Strategy, and any subsequent approved revisions, and achieved a 43.27% reduction in emissions or greater.
(c) Upon final commencement of operation of any low and zero carbon technologies, suitable devices for the monitoring of the low and zero carbon technologies shall have been installed, and the monitored data shall be submitted automatically to a monitoring web-platform at daily intervals for a period of three years from the point of full operation. The data shall be made available to the local planning authority on request for a period of five years.
Reason: In order to ensure that the development makes the fullest contribution to minimising carbon dioxide emissions.
Condition : 5 - Prior to first occupation of the buildings hereby approved, the development shall have been constructed to achieve an internal water use of 105 litres/person/day or less.
Reason: In order to protect and conserve water supplies and resources.
Condition : 6 - No development above ground level shall take place until full details and samples of all materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the development hereby permitted have been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority. Details must include a detailed schedule of materials, a photographic sample board and rendered drawings, elevations and sections at a sufficient scale (1:20 or 1:50) to illustrate how all external materials will appear together.
The details shall include: 
�	Brick/stonework (including brick, stone, masonry, brick panels, feature brick panel, brick framing feature and mortar on-site sample panel, minimum one metre by one metre) including all mortar colours, joint type, brick bond to show how the proposed materials would match those used in the existing building;
�	Cladding materials / render (including specifications where relevant);
�	Tiles / roof covering; including parapet coping / capping materials, dormers and canopies;
�	Window types; and sectional drawings of reveals / sills / head details 
�	Balcony details (including soffits, panels and frame);
�	All privacy measures (including obscure glazing details, privacy screens etc.);
�	Balustrading treatment to balconies and roof areas (including details / sections / materials); and handrails
�	Any other materials/details / fittings to be used (including solar panels, extract vents, rainwater goods, boiler flues etc.), with sections and on-site samples where appropriate
�	Balustrading treatment (including details / sections / materials); and
�	Any other materials / details / fittings to be used (including solar panels, extract vents, boiler flues etc.), with sections and on-site samples where appropriate
The development shall then be carried out in accordance with the approved details and maintained as such thereafter.
Reason: In order to protect the appearance of the area.
Condition : 7 - (A) No development shall take place until details have been submitted to and approved by the local planning authority which demonstrate that:
(i)	At least three of the key elements of the building envelope (external walls, windows roof, upper floor slabs, internal walls, floor finishes/coverings) are to achieve a rating of A+ to D in the Building Research Establishment (BRE) The Green Guide of specification.
(ii)	At least 50% of timber and timber products are to be sourced from accredited Forest Stewardship Council (FSC) or Programme for the Endorsement of Forestry Certification (PEFC) scheme.
(iii)	No construction or insulation materials are to be used which would release toxins into the internal and external environment, including those that deplete stratospheric ozone.
(B) The development shall not be occupied until evidence (e.g. photographs and copies of installation contracts) has been submitted to the local planning authority to demonstrate that the development has been carried out in accordance with the approved details under Part A of this condition. The development shall be maintained in accordance with the approved details at all times thereafter.
Reason: In the interests of sustainable development. 
Condition : 8 - Prior to the occupation of the development, full details of the proposed heat pumps shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. These shall include:
(i)	An estimate of the heating and/or cooling energy (MWh/annum) the heat pumps would provide to the development and the percentage of contribution to the site's heat loads to demonstrate how the heat fraction from heat pump technologies has been maximised. 
(ii)	Details of the Seasonal Coefficient of Performance (SCOP) and/or Seasonal Energy Efficiency ratio (SEER) and how these have been calculated including the expected heat source and heat distribution temperatures (for space heat and hot water) and the distribution loss factor, which shall be calculated based on the above information.
The development shall be carried out in accordance with the approved details.
Reason: To achieve appropriate sustainability standards.
Condition : 9 - Prior to commencement of the development, details of the specifications (regarding power), number, appearance, location, orientation, total area and predicted carbon savings from the photovoltaic panels shall have been submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority to show how the renewable energy carbon savings are to be achieved and maximised. It shall also be demonstrated that the panels would not cause undue glint or glare to overhead air traffic. The photovoltaic panels shall be installed in accordance with the approved details prior to the occupation of the relevant part of the development and retained and maintained as such unless otherwise agreed by the Local Planning Authority. 
Reason: To achieve appropriate sustainability standards and to ensure the development does not endanger the safe movement of aircraft.
Condition : 10 - Prior to commencement of the development, evidence of compliance with the recommendations of the Preliminary Ecological Appraisal (Version 1.0, dated 12/01/2026) hereby approved shall have been submitted to the Local Planning Authority for approval in writing. This shall include the provision of: findings from the further nesting bird check cited in the document; details of any necessary protection measures for nesting birds or other animals during development; details of ecological and habitat enhancements for birds, bats and other species; and a management plan setting out measures for the control and eradication of invasive species across the site (such as Japanese Knotweed), including a schedule of works for continuing these eradication works in the event that the invasive species still remain at the site at the point of occupation of the development. 
Development shall then be carried out in strict accordance with the approved details.
Reason: In the interest of maintaining existing ecology at the site, tackling invasive species found on site, and delivering biodiversity enhancements.
Condition : 11 - The trees that are specified in the submissions hereby approved to be retained shall be protected (with suitable fencing, root protection zone buffers etc.) before commencement of any works on site and throughout the course of the development by methods that conform to the best practice guidance contained in British Standard BS5837: 2012 or any guidance that shall have superseded it.
Reason: In order to ensure a satisfactory appearance of the site and the area and to promote biodiversity. 
Condition : 12 - Notwithstanding any details included in the submitted plans, no development above ground level (except any demolition, site clearance, ground investigation and remediation work) shall take place until details of both hard and soft landscape works have been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority. These details shall include:
(i)	a statement setting out the design objectives and how these will be delivered; 
(ii)	existing and proposed finished levels or contours; 
(iii)	means of enclosure/boundary treatment(s) and retaining structures;
(iv)	vehicle parking layouts and markings; 
(v)	other vehicle and pedestrian access and circulation areas;
(vi)	hard surfacing materials; 
(vii)	minor artefacts and structures (e.g. furniture, refuse or other storage units, signs, lighting, CCTV etc.); 
(viii)	any children's play equipment and surfacing within the shared landscaped area;
(ix)	proposed and existing functional services above and below ground (e.g. drainage, power, communications cables, pipelines etc. indicating alignments, levels, access points, supports as relevant); 
(x)	any renewable energy installations;
(xi)	details of tree planting, including quantity, size, species, and positions or density of all trees to be planted, alongside details of how they will be planted and protected and the proposed times of planting; 
(xii)	planting plans, written specifications (including cultivation and other operations associated with plant and grass establishment) and schedules of plants, noting species, plant sizes and proposed numbers and densities where appropriate and including details of screen planting of an appropriate height along the front boundary; and
(xiii)	an implementation programme (including phasing of work where relevant).
The landscaping works shall comply with the requirements specified in BS 3936 (1992) 'Specification of Nursery Stock Part 1 Trees and Shrubs', and in BS 4428 (1989) 'Recommendations for General Landscap
Condition : 13 - Prior to first use or occupation of the development, a plan indicating the heights (no higher than 0.6 metres within any pedestrian visibility splays), positions, design, materials and type of boundary treatment to be erected shall have been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority; the boundary treatment shall be erected as approved before the development is first brought into use and shall be retained as such thereafter. 
Reason: In order to protect neighbours' living conditions, ensure a satisfactory appearance of the site and area and minimise danger, obstruction and inconvenience to users of the highway and vehicular access.
Condition : 14 - Notwithstanding the submitted Construction Method Statement, no development shall take place until a detailed finalised Construction Logistics Plan (CLP), drafted in accordance with current TfL guidance, has been submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The CLP shall include:
(i)	a site plan (showing the elements set out below);
(ii)	confirmation that a pre-start record of site conditions on the adjoining public highway will be undertaken with Hounslow Highways and a commitment to repair any damage caused;
(iii)	provision for the parking of vehicles of site operatives and visitors;
(iv)	provisions for loading, unloading and storage of plant and materials within the site;
(v)	details of access to the site, including means to control and manage access and egress of vehicles to and from the site for the duration of construction including phasing arrangements;
(vi)	details of the proposed access road and pavements across the site, including at the junction with Staines Road; 
(vii)	details of vehicle routeing from the site to the wider strategic road network;
(viii)	the erection and maintenance of security hoarding including decorative displays and facilities for public viewing, where appropriate;
(ix)	provision of wheel washing facilities at the site exit and a commitment to sweep adjacent roads when required and at the request of the Council;
(x)	a scheme for recycling/disposing of waste resulting from demolition and construction works;
(xi)	measures to ensure the safety of all users of the public highway especially cyclists and pedestrians in the vicinity of the site and especially at the access;
(xii)	commitment to liaise with other contractors in the vicinity of the site to maximise the potential for consolidation and to minimise traffic impacts;
(xiii)	avoidance of peak hours for deliveries and details of a booking system to avoid vehicles waiting on the public highway;
(xiv)	all necessary traffic orders and other permiss
Condition : 15 - No demolition or construction work shall take place on the site except between the hours of 8:00am to 6:00pm on Mondays to Friday and 8:00am to 1:00pm on Saturdays and none shall take place on Sundays and Public Holidays without the prior agreement of the Local Planning Authority. Additionally, HGV deliveries to site during the course of construction will be restricted to 9.30am and 3.00pm on Mondays to Friday, and 9.30am to 1.00pm on Saturdays, and none shall take place on Sundays and Public Holidays without the prior agreement of the Local Planning Authority.
Reason: To ensure that the proposed development does not prejudice the amenities of the locality and to prevent obstruction and inconvenience to users of the public highway.
Condition : 16 - Notwithstanding the submitted Construction Method Statement, and prior to the commencement of the development including any demolition works and site preparation, a detailed and finalised Construction Environment Management Plan (CEMP) shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The CEMP shall provide details of how demolition and construction works are to be undertaken and include:
(i)	The identification of stages of works;
(ii)	measures to mitigate against noise, dust, debris and harmful air pollution, and to avoid run-off and pollutants which could harm nearby waterways during construction;
(iii)	details of working hours, which unless otherwise agreed with the Local Planning Authority shall be limited to 08:00 to 18:00 Monday to Friday and 08:00 to 13:00 on Saturdays);
(iv)	Procedures for maintaining good public relations including complaint management, public consultation and liaison;
(v)	Mitigation measured as defined in BS 5228: Parts 1 and 2: 2009 Noise and Vibration Control on Construction and Open Sites shall be used to minimise noise disturbance from construction works;
(vi)	Measures to control emissions during the construction phase in line with the requirements of the Mayor's Control of Dust and Emissions during Construction and Demolition SPG.
The approved CEMP shall be adhered to throughout the construction period of the development.
Reason: In order to safeguard the amenities of the locality.
Condition : 17 - Notwithstanding the submitted Delivery and Servicing Plan and before the development hereby permitted is first occupied or brought into use, a detailed finalised Delivery and Servicing Plan (including details of vehicle access and egress arrangements and times that servicing shall take place) shall have been submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The details shall accord with current guidance such as that issued by TfL and include measures required to ensure sufficient arrangements (physical as well as managerial) for the servicing, including refuse collection, of all aspects of the development, the timing of hours for deliveries by motor vehicles and a timetable for implementation. The development shall not be carried out otherwise than in accordance with the approved details and shall be maintained for the lifetime of the development, unless the prior written approval of the Local Planning Authority is obtained to any variation.
Reason: In the interests of the safety of pedestrians and vehicles, to protect neighbours' living conditions and to support sustainable transport objectives.
Condition : 18 - The rear hardstanding and means of access shall not be used at any time for the parking of cars or other vehicles, or for purposes other than temporary use for deliveries and servicing associated with the residential and commercial uses hereby approved. 
Reason: In order to ensure effective deliveries and servicing of the site, and to ensure a clear means of pedestrian and cycle access. 
Condition : 19 - Before the development hereby permitted is first occupied or brought into use, the Local Planning Authority shall be informed of the agreed naming and numbering of the proposed dwellings so that arrangements can be put in place to ensure that, with the exception of a person eligible for a disabled person's badge issued pursuant to section 21 of the Chronically Sick and Disabled Persons Act 1970 (or similar legislation), no resident of the development shall obtain a resident's parking permit. Any occupiers of the approved development shall surrender any such permit wrongly issued or held.
Reason: In order to protect the free flow and safety of traffic on nearby highways and to support sustainable transport objectives. 
Condition : 20 - Before the development hereby permitted is first occupied or brought into use, the existing vehicular access onto Lampton Road shall have been permanently closed and kerbs/footway reinstated so that it cannot be used as an access across the pavement, and the front boundary treatment shall have been widened as per the approved drawings. Thereafter, means of vehicle access to the site shall be taken solely from the rear access road off Bulstrode Road, and vehicles shall not access the site from Lampton Road at any time. Notwithstanding the provisions of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development Order) 1995 (or any order revoking or re-enacting that order), no other means of access shall be formed to the site. 
Reason: In order to enhance the pedestrian environment and to confine vehicular access to the permitted points in order to ensure that the development does not prejudice the free flow of traffic or highway safety along the adjacent highway.
Condition : 21 - Prior to first use or occupation of the development, finalised details of the arrangements for the storing of waste and recycled materials (including details of how the placing of waste and recycled materials in a suitable location for collection would be undertaken and managed and demonstrating compliance with the Council's Recycling and Refuse Guidelines SPD) shall have been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority. The development shall not be carried out otherwise than in accordance with the approved details.
All refuse and recycling bins and delivery carts in association with the approved development are to be stored within the approved facilities at all times and only brought out when deliveries are being made or refuse collected.
Reason: In order to ensure adequate provision for waste and recycling and to prevent obstruction to access outside collection times.
Condition : 22 - Prior to first use or occupation of the development full details (including manufacturers' specifications) of secure covered cycle parking facilities that accord with the West London Cycle Parking Guidance for the occupants of, and visitors to, the development shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The approved facilities shall be fully implemented and made available for use before the development is first occupied or brought into use, The approved facilities shall be thereafter retained for use at all times without obstruction.
Reason: In order to support sustainable transport objectives.
Condition : 23 - The development hereby approved shall be carried out in accordance with the mitigation measures proposed in the submitted 'Air Quality Assessment' (dated P9550-R2-V1, Version 1, dated 30/01/2026) during construction and operational phases. All works which form part of the finished scheme, including any remedial measures, shall be completed before the development is first occupied and shall be retained in operation thereafter. 
Reason: In order to ensure that the future users of the development or existing surrounding occupiers will not be exposed to harmful air quality.
Condition : 24 - The development hereby approved shall be carried out in accordance with the mitigation measures proposed in the submitted 'Noise Impact Assessment Report' (P9550-R1-V1, Version 1, dated 30/01/2026) during construction and operational phases. All works which form part of the finished scheme, including any remedial measures, shall be completed before the development is first occupied and shall be retained in operation thereafter. 
Reason: To ensure that the amenity of occupiers of the development site is not adversely affected by noise from transport and other noise sources.
Condition : 25 - The ground floor commercial premises hereby approved shall not be used outside the hours specified below:
Monday to Saturdays: 08:00 - 19:00
Sundays and Public Holidays: Closed 
Reason: In order to protect neighbours' living conditions. 
Supporting Note: 
If this approved use requires a trading licence from the Council (for example, because you intend to sell alcohol or offer entertainment) you should obtain this before you start to trade and note that the Licensing Panel will enquire about and wish you to disclose the terms of this permission and will likely align the terms of the licence with those set out here.  If your licence application seeks to exceed these hours, you will first need to have sought and obtained formally a variation to this condition by making a planning application.   
Condition : 26 - The premises shall be used for Class E commercial purposes only, with the exception of the following uses, which shall not be permitted:
�	E(b): Sale of food and drink for consumption (mostly on the premises)
�	E(d): Indoor sport, recreation or fitness (not involving motorised vehicles or firearms)
�	E(f): Creche, day nursery or day centre (not including a residential use)
The premises shall be used for no other purpose within the Schedule to the Town and Country Planning (Use Classes) Order 1987 (as amended), including any provision equivalent to that Class in any statutory instrument revoking and re-enacting that Order with or without modification.
Reason: The Council is satisfied that the use hereby permitted (with exclusions) would not result in detriment to adjoining properties but would wish to control future changes of use within the same Use Class to protect nearby land uses and the character of the area.
Condition : 27 - (a)	The development shall achieve 'Secured by Design' accreditation awarded by the Design-Out Crime Officer from the Metropolitan Police Service on behalf of the Association of Chief Police Officers (ACPO).
(b)	Prior to first use, accreditation will be evidenced as achieved and evidence of such accreditation will need to be submitted and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority.
Reason: To tackle crime and disorder and to ensure that the development provides a safe and secure environment.
